# Phase 3 remoting transport audit — 20260928T021700Z

- Continued the local Phase 3 audit; kept `20260927T085045Z.rlog` and all earlier logs unchanged. Re-read the complete coding-rust skill and both complete Phase 3 plans; no plan edits.
- Implemented/corroborated Java-equivalent inbound processor dispatch details in the working tree: exact processor/executor registration is captured and `reject_request()` runs at decode/dispatch before queueing; a `reject_request()` panic now propagates to normal connection failure cleanup (EXCEPTION, CLOSE, pending failure) instead of silently terminating the Tokio task. Added/confirmed regression coverage including `p3_reject_request_panic_closes_generation_and_fails_pending_calls`, retired-generation inbound response routing, nullable after-hook response, and before-hook failure intermediate response remark.
- Reviewed Java `NettyRemotingAbstract.processRequestCommand`, `TlsHelper.buildSslContext`, and `NettyRemotingAbstract.NettyEventExecutor` directly. Event queue capacity/admission is mapped (10001 entries); FIFO ordering is covered; worker polling, scheduling, shutdown/drain and thread lifecycle remain user-accepted Tokio runtime differences. Java `rejectRequest()` throwing reaches the client exception handler/close path.
- Identified a remaining unresolved TLS parity item: Java verified mode with `tls.client.authServer=true` and no explicit trustCertPath lets JSSE use its default trust store, while Rust uses `rustls_native_certs` platform roots. Existing verified loopback tests use explicit CA; they do not prove default trust-source equivalence. Recorded this as an unresolved gate blocker in the inventory, ADR and compatibility summary; did not claim it accepted or equivalent.
- Validation after the rejection-panic fix: `cargo test --workspace --offline -- --test-threads=1` PASS (all workspace/unit/transport/doc tests); `cargo fmt --all --check` PASS; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings` PASS; `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py` PASS; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test` PASS; `git diff --check` PASS. Also re-ran `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --test transport --locked` and `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --locked`; both PASS.
